<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 13.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 13.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for May 13.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    May    212.00    215.50    216.00     219.50</p>
<p>    Jun    208.00    211.50    212.00     218.50</p>
<p>    Jul    205.00    208.50    209.00     217.50</p>
<p>    Aug    202.50    206.00    206.50     215.50</p>
<p>    Sept   202.50    206.00    206.50     215.50</p>
<p>    Oct    203.50    207.00    207.50     216.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased A$0.50 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	185.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  160.50	    Port Adelaide	 161.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     160.75	    Port Giles	    162.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	158.50	    Wallaroo		160.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    157.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     160.50	    Port Lincoln	  163.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   161.00	    Thevenard	     158.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 162.00	     Esperance	    165.25</p>
<p>    Portland	161.00	     Albany		 166.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    168.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    166.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
